      "knowledge_point_id": "49251196-c06b-5718-82e6-5ed9450301af",
      "knowledge_point": "Finding the Complement of a Set Given Using Ellipsis Notation",
      "problem": "If $U=\\{-20,-18,-16,-14,…,20\\}$ is the universal set and $A=\\{-20,-16,-12,-8,…,20\\},$ then $\\overset{―}{A}=$",
      "worked_solution": "The complement of $A,$ denoted $\\overset{―}{A},$ consists of every element in the universal set $U$ that is not in the set $A.$\n\nThe universal set $U$ consists of the even integers $-20$ through $20,$ while the set $A$ consists of the multiples of $4$ from $-20$ through $20.$\n\nSo, the only elements of $U$ that are not in $A$ are the even integers from $-18$ through $18$ that are not multiples of $4.$\n\nTherefore, the complement of $A$ is\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{A}=\\{-18,-14,-10,-6,-2,2,6,10,14,18\\}.\n$$",
